eve Hilton", "source": "Los Angeles Times", "published": "2026-08-10T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPMm5FR1c2M3gwMnByNWFmTHVsbWhidEx3cUoxbTBrVHhGczF2QXZURndPMmZ3MVFCZEpERDNoYTN6TjZzaVRQTWhiLTZ2NjQ3ekFwQXJrd21jSnprYXJoQldmdkRaNkR5NkpNdFVvQ3RHVHZGeEtXYUlYN0k5cWU2UU1HRFptSDhlVmduYW5uR0ZpaXdqOHVRTTE5cEdmczRqcjh1em1sWENXUnV5ZW9IY0JR?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 14.8, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 22.84, "poll_sd": 4.94, "poll_weight": 0.54, "fundamentals": {"margin": 13.0, "lean": 9.0, "environment": 4.1, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -0.1}, "rating_margin": 16.0, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 5.95, "baseline_margin": 19.14, "analyst_adjustment": 1.86, "key_factors": ["Becerra leads September polls by 22-25 points among likely voters in a D+12 state", "All six expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column", "Prediction markets price Becerra's win probability at 95-96 percent", "Hilton's slight fundraising edge and affordability message have not narrowed the gap"], "rationale": "Becerra holds a 22-plus-point lead in the latest independent surveys, all six raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and markets price him around 95 percent. Hilton's fundraising advantage and affordability pitch have not dented a lead that has widened through September.", "watch": "A major late-breaking event or a flood of outside spending behind Hilton's affordability campaign could tighten the race, but he would need a historic swing to overcome a twenty-point deficit.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gavin Newsom (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "California's open governor's race pits Democrat Xavier Becerra against Republican Steve Hilton, with the seat vacated by term limits. The state's strong Democratic lean frames the contest, and every recent independent poll shows Becerra ahead by 22 to 25 points among likely voters, a gap that has widened since summer. All six expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets price Becerra's chances around 95 percent.\n\nHilton has slightly out-raised Becerra and has campaigned on affordability, schools, and 'common sense' change, themes that speak to voter concern about the cost of living. So far those efforts have not moved the numbers; September surveys show him losing ground instead. Becerra's narrower cash position is a minor caveat in a race where the structural margin remains very large.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}]}